## @PRODUCT_NAME@ @VERSION@

@PRODUCT_SUMMARY@

This pre-alpha build includes **Help → Create Local Bug Report**. The IDE
saves a ZIP locally with diagnostic information and images of its own windows.
You choose whether to share it. See the [release guide](https://github.com/@REPOSITORY@/blob/@TAG@/docs/release.md)
for supported systems, installation and known limitations. Check downloaded files
against `SHA256SUMS` before installing.

- macOS arm64 / Intel: `@SLUG@-@VERSION@-macos-{aarch64,x86_64}.dmg` or `.tar.gz`.
  Open the DMG and drag `@APP@` to Applications. Builds are ad hoc signed,
  not notarized; Gatekeeper may require System Settings → Privacy & Security →
  Open Anyway. The archive includes the same application bundle.
- Windows x64: `@SLUG@-@VERSION@-windows-x86_64.setup.exe` offers current-user
  and all-users installation; the latter requires administrator privileges.
  The `.zip` includes a `data` directory for portable profiles; installers do
  not. This does not isolate projects, external tools or Windows-managed data.
  SmartScreen and enterprise policies can block unsigned applications.
- Linux arm64 / x64: `.tar.gz`, `.deb`, and `.AppImage` packages built on Ubuntu
  24.04. These need the native graphics libraries listed in the release guide;
  the AppImage is not a promise of compatibility with every distribution.

The application is `@IDE@`. Python tooling and its debugpy helper ship only with
the Python product. `install-@SLUG@.sh` is an inspectable checksum-checking user
installer for the tar archive; `@SLUG@.rb` is a Homebrew formula template rendered
for this release. No Homebrew tap is published automatically.

Preview workflow artifacts are for testing. Creation of a draft release and its
publication are separate maintainer steps after cross-platform checks and build
acceptance. No auto-update or unattended migration is included.
